        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{5}{2},\\ y=3$",
          "worked": "Multiply (1) by 4.\n$$\\begin{align*}8x+12y&=56\\quad(3)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (2) from (3).\n$$\\begin{align*}(8x+12y)-(8x-5y)&=56-5\\\\17y&=51\\\\y&=3\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1).\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+3(3)&=14\\\\2x+9&=14\\\\2x&=5\\\\x&=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
